    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the SGD 4.50 no-show fee stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.60.\n\nFacts found. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02721) shows the driver accepted at 15:03:58, tapped 'I'm Here' at 15:11:34, the 180-second free-wait timer started at 15:11:36, and the driver cancelled at 15:18:15 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02721, weight 1.0) places the driver a minimum of 0 m from the pickup pin and shows 41 consecutive fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius over one continuous 400-second run from 15:11:34 to 15:18:14. The rider's own device track sits 725-732 m from the pin throughout, with no fix inside the 100 m rider-presence radius, and the rider sent no message.\n\nApplying the policy. POL-NS-02's arrival test is satisfied: the trace supplies far more than the three consecutive in-radius fixes it requires, and the pre-pass geometry returns 41 qualifying in-radius fixes. The rider argued that because this export reports no horizontal accuracy, the arrival test is not affirmatively made out and limbs (b) and (c) fail. I do not accept that. The policy's own integrity block says a fix with no reported accuracy is treated as of unknown accuracy and is neither counted nor excluded by the 25 m filter, and I must not recompute the derived geometry: the arrival test runs and is met, so the 400 s dwell it measures is established. POL-NS-05 is not engaged - at the arrival timestamp the driver was at the pin (0 m, not over 300 m) and stationary (distinct speeds include 0.0 kph, not 15 kph or more) - so the 'I'm Here' marker is true and the waiting clock needs no recomputation. POL-NS-01 therefore holds in full: (a) arrival event present; (b) in-geofence at and before it; (c) 400 s continuous dwell against the 180 s free waiting period in force; (d) terminated by the driver with the valid RIDER_NO_SHOW code after the dwell elapsed, with no boarding event. POL-NS-06 gives no shortfall (400 s against 180 s; shortfall -220 s), and POL-NS-03 does not govern, because the driver's stationary fixes are inside the radius, not outside it. POL-NS-08 is not engaged: 92 fixes at a 10 s cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, termination corroborated by the last in-geofence fix, chat count matching the trip record, and the SGD 4.50 fare line reconciling to the fee in force. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: limb (a) fails (the only chat message is the driver's own, at 15:11:54) and limb (c) fails affirmatively on the rider's own track, so POL-NS-11's undecidable route is not open.\n\nMoney. POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee in force = SGD 3.60 (the fare breakdown's own driver_compensation figure; the net figure, not the rider's SGD 6.61 gross). The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below 4, and 1 termination over 126 completed trips is 0.0079, below 0.08; both limbs are required. Compensation is therefore paid and the rider's charge stands. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 figure (the amount the ruling moves, not a second payment).\n\nThe rider's POL-GEN-01 point is well taken: the lifetime counters prior_no_show_flags and prior_disputes_filed are context only, and no adverse inference was drawn from them. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02721-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) is citable as absent, but nothing turns on it - there is no shortfall for POL-NS-06(i) to cure. The driver's POL-NS-06 claim was discarded at the mechanical stage for citing that missing advisory without naming its issue code, and it changes nothing either. No escalation applies: confidence is well above the 0.70 floor and no POL-NS-09 trigger fires. No clause produces a referral. The monetary effect (SGD 3.60) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold and is executed automatically on issue."
  },
